    /// animation, a bad joint name or a turn that is not three numbers, and a RangeError for no keys or
    /// more than 32, times that do not start at 0 and rise up to 60 s, more than 32 joints in a key, a
    /// lift out of -1 to 0.5, a lashTrack out of its ranges, or more than 2000 bytes as sent. (Server
    /// only.)
    /// </summary>
    /// <param name="options">`{ keys: [{ time, pose: { &lt;joint name&gt;: [x, y, z] }, lift?, lash? }], blend?: 'spline' | 'smooth' | 'linear', loop?: boolean, lashTrack?: { rate, length, frames } }`: the key animation. `lashTrack` shapes the whip's lash at its own times instead of the keys' lash: `rate` frames a second from the start (1 to 60), the lash's `length` in metres (0.1 to 6) in equal segments, and `frames` (2 to 600), each `[yaw, pitch, ...]` in degrees for every segment from the handle's tip out (2 to 16 segments), yaw toward the handle's right side (within 180) and pitch toward its up side (within 90), or with `space: 'body'` in the body's frame (yaw from its forward toward its right, pitch toward its up: the lash keeps its way when the wrist turns); between two frames each segment's way is blended, so the lash keeps its length, and a looping animation's frames go round. Each turn is in degrees about the joint's parent's axes; the first key is at 0 s. A key's `lift` raises the hips that many metres, below 0 lowers them (bent knees on the ground), -1 to 0.5, blended toward the next key that lifts them. A key's `lash` gives the player's whip its lash's shape: 1 to 16 points `[along, right, up]` in metres from the handle's tip in the handle's frame, each within 6 m; while keys shape it, the lash takes those shapes, blended key to key, instead of moving by physics, the same on every client. The blend is spline and loop is true by default. Pass null to stop it.</param>
